  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-t1658\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n               \n                <div class=\"tutorial\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Modeling Assumptions</span></div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"t1658\">?</div>\n                    </div>                    \n    \n                    <p>In this topic, we made the following assumptions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>All objects are treated like a <strong>particle</strong>, a small point with no length, width, or height.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>All objects move vertically down in a straight line, so acceleration due to gravity is taken as positive.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The only acceleration the objects have is due to gravity, and any other forces (such as wind resistance) are negligible.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n           \n                </div>        \n                    \n            </div>",
